list-item.p:
Precision: The proportion of correctly predicted positive instances among all instances predicted as positive.\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$ {\mathrm{Precision}} = \frac{{{\mathrm{True}}\;{\mathrm{Positives}}}}{{{\text{True }}\;{\mathrm{Positives}} + {\mathrm{False}}\;{\mathrm{Positives}}}} $$\end{document}

Recall (sensitivity): The proportion of correctly predicted positive instances among all actual positive instances.\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$ {\mathrm{Recall}} = \frac{{{\mathrm{True}}\;{\mathrm{Positives}}}}{{{\text{True }}\;{\mathrm{Positives}} + {\mathrm{False}}\;{\mathrm{Negatives}}}} $$\end{document}

F1-score: The harmonic mean of precision and recall, providing a single metric to balance both.\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$ {\mathrm{F}}1 - {\mathrm{Score}} = 2 \times \frac{{{\mathrm{Precision}} \times {\mathrm{Recall}}}}{{{\mathrm{Precision}} + {\mathrm{Recall}}}} $$\end{document}

Area under the ROC curve (AUC): AUC represents the area under the ROC curve, which plots the true positive rate (TPR) against the false positive rate (FPR) at various classification thresholds. It measures the model’s ability to discriminate between positive and negative classes.\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$ {\mathrm{AUC}} = \mathop \smallint \limits_{0}^{1} TPR\left( {FPR} \right)d\left( {FPR} \right) $$\end{document}

Average precision (AP): AP summarizes the precision–recall curve by computing the weighted mean of precision values achieved at different recall levels, with the increase in recall used as the weight.\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$ {\mathrm{AP}} = { }\mathop \sum \limits_{n} \left( {R_{n} - R_{n - 1} } \right) \cdot P_{n} $$\end{document}where \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$P_{n}$$\end{document} and \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$R_{n}$$\end{document} denote the precision and recall at the n-th threshold, respectively.
